# Secrets — never commit. .env was historically tracked and leaked an
# OpenAI key (caught by GitHub push protection) plus Moz / Diffbot / AWS /
# Perplexity / Tinify credentials that leaked silently. History was
# rewritten on 2026-05-16 to scrub .env from every commit.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# Databases — the binary recipes.db is NOT tracked (git can't delta a 29MB+
# binary, so every commit stored a fresh full copy). The GZIPPED logical dump
# recipes.sql.gz IS tracked and serves as the git-side backup + restore source
# (plain recipes.sql grew past GitHub's 100 MB file limit, so backup_db.py now
# writes .gz — ~5x smaller; restore: gunzip -c recipes.sql.gz | sqlite3 new.db).
# The live .db is backed up to ADAM/GitHub via bcc_backup.bat. media.db holds
# regenerable binary (page screenshots) and is never tracked.
recipes.db
recipes.db-wal
recipes.db-shm
# The uncompressed dump is never tracked (too big); only recipes.sql.gz is.
recipes.sql
media.db
media.db-wal
media.db-shm
# page_cache.db: raw harvest-page fetch cache (gzip HTML) — regenerable, kept out
# of git/recipes.sql so it never bloats the tracked DB dump (see page_cache.py).
page_cache.db
page_cache.db-wal
page_cache.db-shm
# training.db: byproduct ML-training capture (is-recipe samples + future label
# streams) accumulated as a free side effect of running the harvest/batch
# pipeline. Regenerable-as-we-run, never source; see docs/corpus-ml-strategy.md.
training.db
training.db-wal
training.db-shm
# Enrich's own reference DB (enrich/data/enrich.db). Canonical at runtime, but
# regenerable from the committed JSON seeds (KA chart + curated_liquids.json),
# so the binary itself is never tracked.
enrich/data/*.db
enrich/data/*.db-wal
enrich/data/*.db-shm
enrich/data/*.generated.json

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Claude Code state
.claude/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# JetBrains per-machine state (project files stay tracked; data-source
# files and workspace UI state are machine-specific)
.idea/dataSources.local.xml
.idea/dataSources/
.idea/data_source_mapping.xml
.idea/workspace.xml

# Recipe-pipeline runtime artifacts: every bookmarklet capture writes a PNG
# into input/, and image extracts write there too. These are inputs to the
# pipeline, not source to track. Subdirectories (e.g. input/pipeline/) are
# tracked normally — only loose image files at input/ root are ignored.
input/*.png
input/*.jpg
input/*.jpeg
# SEMrush Top-Pages / Organic-Pages exports the curator drops here for the
# publisher harvest (see project_backlinks_source). Pipeline inputs, not source.
input/*.xlsx
input/*.csv
input/pipeline/__pycache__/
input/__pycache__/
extract/__pycache__/
to_markdown/__pycache__/

# Generated outputs (image gen, batch results)
generated-images/
batches/
# generated/ holds AI-generated + user-uploaded recipe images. Runtime
# accumulating state, not source — created on demand by /images and
# /recipes/<id>/generate-image. App auto-mkdir's at startup.
generated/

# Logs / temp DB tools
recipe_server.log
recipe_database.db
recipes.sqbpro
# Daily scheduled-backup log (bcc_backup_scheduled.bat); runtime, not source.
backup.log
# uvicorn stdio is redirected to these files by bcc_start.bat —
# regenerated every restart, never source.
uvicorn_stdout.log
uvicorn_stderr.log
uvicorn_stderr_new.log
# Same, for detached agent-launched restarts.
uvicorn_stdout_agent.log
uvicorn_stderr_agent.log
# Per-job runtime logs from the async job system. The dishes form
# links to the latest via /logs/<filename>; never source.
logs/

# pycache that the existing entries missed
scripts/__pycache__/
intake/__pycache__/

# Loose capture artifacts that landed in repo root
/momsAsparagusAuGratin.png

# DataForSEO API creds (local only)
scripts/.dataforseo.env

# Scheduler tick log (runtime, like uvicorn_*_agent.log)
jobs_schedule.log

# Stray IDE-created empty SQLite (JetBrains data source)
identifier.sqlite

# RealRank run outputs (product brief .json/.md/.raw.txt). Regenerated by the
# realrank_research job; the code is source, the briefs are results.
docs/RealRank/out/
docs/RealRank/realrank_out.*

# RealRank posting preview (a copy dropped into forms/ so it can be viewed at
# /forms/_realrank_preview.html; the real output lives in docs/RealRank/out/).
forms/_realrank_preview.html

# Curation experiment: cached source docs + raw replies (regenerable)
experiments/curate/cache/
experiments/curate/out/
